# The accounts whose id is recorded in the image, and the ids they must keep.
#
# Only accounts that own something need to be here: ownership is stored as a
# number, so if the id moves between two builds a machine that upgraded
# between them disagrees with what the image ships. Everything else may be
# allocated freely, which is also what the Fedora packaging guidelines and
# NixOS ids.nix say. Package maintainer scripts take whichever id is free, so
# the build writes these entries before installing anything, and
# `bootc-ubuntu-imagectl finalize` fails if the built image disagrees.
#
# Same format as /etc/group. Add an entry when a package starts shipping a
# setgid binary or a mode-restricted directory owned by a new account.
_ssh:x:101:
messagebus:x:995:
